id: pm-rust-admission-previews
title: Preview canonical item admission without native tracker writes
description: Bounded Rust SDK and CLI preflight for canonical item intents using the native mutation path.
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: admission,"gh:unbraind/pm-rust#132",native,oracle
created_at: "2026-10-29T04:13:00.543Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T19:24:25.367Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Unsupported intent kinds refuse before any write; admitted and refused fixtures match the published TypeScript previewItemMutations oracle for the declared slice; every byte and row limit is reported.
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[39]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T04:23:45.667Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses shared native create/update document preparation and the existing native status registry. Preview has no persistence phase: ordered candidate state stays in memory, independent row failures retain diagnostics, and a refused target suppresses later same-target intents. Hard input/source/row/directory/depth/output ceilings are reported. The declared slice is progressive explicit-scope creates and scalar updates; custom field/type workflows and complex lifecycle transitions refuse explicitly. Published oracle remains repo-pinned at 2026.10.21 per package policy; current registry pm is 2026.10.28. Unsupported operation kinds refuse before tracker discovery. No transaction-lock isolation or future commit guarantee is claimed."
  "2026-10-29T04:40:19.636Z",codex-agent,"Local acceptance passed: 3 integration tests including 33 published oracle cases and 500 seeded state-preservation sequences; the initial 9 native unit tests also passed, including 500 seeded preview-versus-actual-apply sequences and step-boundary interleaving. Additional I/O and rendering boundary coverage is being measured. Follow-up pm-rust-admission-schema tracks expansion beyond the explicit first contract; these cases currently return typed refusals rather than implied admission."
  "2026-10-29T04:57:57.546Z",codex-agent,"Live sibling overlap refresh confirms CSV owns external CSV schemas/imports at pm-csv main 1c13ab7d154a12d81f7ad4c5d870635a41f56d23, and Beads owns external JSONL import/export and source snapshots at pm-beads main 7f3762d942caeb2fb736086132a17268a4e6f622. The Rust feature adds no external-format parser. Expanded oracle fixtures cover every built-in create type, canonical custom active/draft statuses, scalar updates, tags, missing fields and conflicts. Core accepts metadata-only empty updates while the native write contract requires an explicit scalar replacement; this boundary is documented and remains outside the declared parity slice."
  "2026-10-29T05:17:34.788Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert verified in a disposable non-git copy: replacing only Workspace::preview_item_mutations with its unsupported-capability refusal makes admission_cli_is_native_bounded_and_never_writes fail at runtime (0 passed, 1 failed). The original implementation was never edited during this proof. The linked native acceptance commands are now rebuilding and verifying the fixed implementation through pm test --run --progress. Follow-up pm-rust-admission-schema is independently scoped under the native implementation epic so it does not block verification of this declared slice."
  "2026-10-29T05:45:10.339Z",codex-agent,"Final local evidence: all 3 linked commands passed through pm test (18 tests total, 0 skipped, 0 failed); clippy all-targets/all-features and format checks passed. The real-data command certified 89 public tracker items at 1af599038dcbbb59b5d15092b30d03c30b52f86f. Archived corpus: 184 files / 4698201 bytes; SDK preparation added 8 scratch runtime files before freezing 192 files read-only. Native observations each read 909472 source bytes and visited 99 entries. Four intents yielded 3 admitted and 1 missing-target refusal; input 427 bytes, JSON output 1090 bytes including newline, debug wall time 859 ms. Every frozen byte and the whole SDK-read corpus remained unchanged. Native PATH was empty and the tracker had no git repository. Full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to CI at unchanged thresholds; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-29T05:59:20.761Z",codex-agent,"Local strict health is not certified: the inherited extension host-version skew and clone-local merge-driver drift are recorded on existing follow-up pm-rust-vuwe. Native acceptance, clippy, format and changelog evidence remain passing. PR 132 is ready for review; CI must establish final-head npm/Bun aggregate and coverage results. The health finding does not authorize history repair or driver work."
  "2026-10-29T06:25:58.665Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI run 40826931277 passed the macOS and Linux Rust jobs. The macOS aggregate completed both Rust passes but refused the unchanged 100 percent coverage gate because the CLI propagation of a Workspace preview failure was unexercised at src/main.rs:740. Add an invalid discovered-tracker fixture to the existing CLI stdio regression; no product behavior or coverage threshold changes are required."
  "2026-10-29T06:31:18.988Z",codex-agent,"The invalid discovered-tracker CLI regression passes with stable and instrumented builds. A focused nightly branch-coverage run records 1 hit in the previously missing error-propagation region at src/main.rs:740; the linked CLI command also passes through pm test --run --only-index 3 --progress. All-target/all-feature clippy passes. This changes only test coverage, not product behavior or thresholds. Fresh final-head aggregates must still pass; any outstanding run will be reported at the existing CI wait cutoff."
  "2026-10-29T06:52:36.937Z",codex-agent,"Resumed review fixes. Main is already included. Audit classes: mutation authorization must be shared by preview and apply; configured closure readiness must hold independently of status roles. Will cover strict foreign ownership, custom workflow closure statuses and public SDK parity, plus behavioral revert proofs. No additional non-blocking findings appear in the supplied review instructions or public PR review records."
  "2026-10-29T07:11:26.023Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: scalar update and annotation apply paths lacked strict ownership enforcement; both now share the native author/principal guard used by preview preparation. Existing claim/release, close, lifecycle and linked-collection paths already enforce ownership. Closure readiness follows the configured close target independently of roles, for creates and scalar updates. Missing optional registry files now preserve embedded settings rather than override them with defaults. Preview JSON/TOON use the same verdict. Product is a native Rust crate/binary; npm and Bun entries invoke native release gates rather than distribute an SDK loader. Read-only public main tracker validation: 89 items, 184 archived files, 4698201 archived bytes, 192 frozen files, 909472 source bytes and 99 entries per observation, 427 input bytes and 1090 output bytes; 3 admitted/1 refused, all source bytes and SDK read-back unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T07:15:04.083Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable non-git source copy, replacing only validate_scalar_owner with success makes the adversarial governance property fail (0 passed, 1 failed; foreign update admitted). Separately replacing only validate_scalar_closure with success fails the same property (0 passed, 1 failed; admitted instead of close_reason_required). Original source remains fixed; final focused and aggregate runs rebuild it. The previous active-role closed-create must-allow assertion was corrected to the published oracle refusal, retaining explicit-reason and disabled-requirement must-allow cases. Expanded corpus also found pinned previewItemMutations admits active-role configured closure updates; those remain outside the declared native scalar slice and are tested independently as refusals, rather than claiming oracle agreement for them."
  "2026-10-29T07:22:32.616Z",codex-agent,"Oracle correction to the earlier registry-fallback hypothesis: pm CLI 2026.10.21 supplies default registries when optional schema files are missing, even with embedded overrides. Capture and apply now call the SAME native default_schema helper; the incorrect embedded-only fallback change was removed. The expanded oracle includes the missing-file case, while configured-close properties explicitly write the effective workflow file. No existing audit events were removed. The first linked run found this discrepancy and hit the default library-test timeout; rerunning all linked tests with --timeout 1200."
  "2026-10-29T07:26:36.564Z",codex-agent,"Fixed-source focused verification passes through pinned pm test --run --progress --timeout 1200: 4 integration tests (130 published SDK cases plus 24 native closure-update JSON/TOON refusals), 16 library tests and 1 CLI stdio test; 3 linked commands passed, zero skipped. Clippy all targets/features passes with warnings denied. Persisted 1200-second timeouts for the two long linked commands; no assertions or thresholds reduced. Full npm and Bun gates run sequentially with at most two build jobs and two test threads under neutral Git identity."
  "2026-10-29T08:39:50.097Z",codex-agent,"Local npm aggregate reached 524 passed/1 failed/0 ignored, then stopped at the pre-existing five-second relationship packet child deadline. Isolated retry reproduces the same signature. Reused existing pm-rust-local-packet-deadline, whose main history already documents this local condition and passing full CI. No orientation source, test or limit changed. Both admission review classes and focused linked tests remain passing; exact-head CI is required for full release and coverage certification."
  "2026-10-29T08:40:30.732Z",codex-agent,"Tally correction: the actual npm aggregate log contains 18 completed Rust groups: 576 passed, 1 failed, 0 ignored. The earlier 524 figure omitted completed groups. The only failure remains the existing local packet child deadline; no assertions or bounds changed."
  "2026-10-29T08:42:41.909Z",codex-agent,"Final-source read-only public tracker validation passes again: 89 items, 184 archived files/4698201 bytes, 192 frozen files, 909472 source bytes and 99 entries per observation, 427 input bytes/1090 output bytes, 3 admitted/1 refused, measured debug wall time 1944 ms. Every source byte and complete SDK read-back remain unchanged; native PATH contains neither Git nor Node."
  "2026-10-29T10:22:25.998Z",codex-agent,"Re-review classes fixed through shared native apply preparation: strict foreign ownership on all six scalar fields and annotations, including no-op/stale-lock-force attempts; configured close-reason requirements independent of roles. SDK readSettings confirms explicit true/false and missing-default true across four presets. Focused pm commands pass 4 integration +16 library +1 CLI; nightly instrumented admission filter passes 26 tests. Admission module coverage is 100 percent lines/functions/regions/branches (571/57/775/132); new guard source regions execute. Crash-check passes 82/82, no skips/todos/cancellations, plus typecheck/lint and 20-receipt/36-commit evidence gates. Cargo audit passes with the existing allowed maintenance warning. Local npm and Bun full attempts each finish 18 groups with 576 passed/1 known packet-deadline failure/0 ignored; existing follow-up reused, no bound weakened. Exact-head CI release/coverage evidence will be maintained in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/132 with the queue's bounded wait. No extra substantive non-blocking review findings were supplied or publicly available. Own claim will now be released; items remain open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T11:16:33.494Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 class audit: captured bytes must be immutable and match every derived view, including aliased schema paths; admission targets must obey the same filename and embedded-ID identity rules as native SDK lookup. Main is already included and the worktree was clean. Will add shared-path interleavings and SDK-resolution property cases, retain all earlier governance regressions, and prove each fix by behavioral revert. No additional substantive public inline findings were found."
  "2026-10-29T11:49:11.869Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 behavioral revert proofs: four independent disposable non-git source copies each compiled and failed the targeted adversarial test (0 passed, 1 failed): removing snapshot reuse returns stale ok=true after shared-schema role replacement; disabling filename identity validation admits unresolved records; removing mutation-locator validation permits an alias update; disabling recovery validation replays an invalid create journal. Fixed sources remain intact. Class audit covers shared settings/schema aliases, SDK and CLI JSON/TOON previews, targeted native reads/writes, and create/update recovery. Legacy list/export reads remain compatible. No additional non-blocking finding was present in the supplied round-2 review."
  "2026-10-29T12:00:56.704Z",codex-agent,"Fixed-source linked verification passed all four commands: 5 integration, 20 admission library, 1 CLI boundary and 1 recovery test (27 total, zero failed or ignored). Published oracle covers 132 parity cases plus 12 independent filename-identity fixtures, with JSON/TOON and restored canonical targets. Pinned pm reports test-result tracking disabled; this comment retains the measured result without copying sandbox paths. Fresh origin/main fetch remains fully contained in this branch (no merge needed)."
  "2026-10-29T12:06:17.910Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 class rules: derived schema views retain one immutable observed byte image; every targeted preview/write/recovery must resolve the physical filename and embedded ID identically to SDK get. Audit searched every decode/read and snapshot map in the crate; legacy search/list/export stay permissive for inspection, while all mutations share the locator. Two further independent reverts compile and fail behaviorally (0 passed, 1 failed each): removing only admission's filename check admits an unresolvable target; removing only recovery's before-image identity check replays over a wrong-ID image despite a matching saved hash. Together with the four earlier reverts, all six guards have direct fail-on-revert evidence. Fixed sources are being rebuilt for mutation and release gates."
  "2026-10-29T12:09:38.584Z",codex-agent,"After all disposable reverts, rebuilt fixed sources and ran cargo +1.90.0 test --locked -j 2 --lib mutation::tests -- --test-threads=2: 116 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored. This verifies existing create/update/comment/claim/close and collection recovery behavior alongside the new identity refusal cases. Next are unchanged nightly branch instrumentation and serial neutral-home npm/Bun release gates, capped at two workers."
  "2026-10-29T12:20:40.594Z",codex-agent,"Nightly scoped verification passed 32 tests (26 library, 1 binary, 5 integration), zero failures or ignored tests. cargo +nightly-2026-08-06 llvm-cov --locked --branch --lib --bin pm-rust --test admission_contract -j 2 --json --output-path coverage-report.json -- admission --test-threads=2 measured src/admission.rs at 100%: 576 lines, 58 functions, 786 regions, 134 branches. Shared filename and recovery validation helpers executed with no uncovered helper source regions. This is scoped evidence; the unchanged full npm/Bun and global coverage gates remain required. Neutral-home npm aggregate is running first."
  "2026-10-29T12:55:58.192Z",codex-agent,"The neutral-home npm aggregate reached 24 Rust groups: 653 passed, 1 failed, 0 ignored. Unlike earlier attempts, all 32 orientation cases passed, including the existing packet deadline. The failure was an established ownership contract: an aliased filename absent from the logical ID index must return ItemNotFound, while the new locator returned InvalidItemDocument. Kept the existing test unchanged and mapped only filename-identity mismatches to ItemNotFound in the shared mutation locator; malformed item decoding retains its original error. Re-running focused read/identity tests before resuming full gates."
  "2026-10-29T13:00:07.621Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility correction verified: all 18 existing read_contract tests pass unchanged. Rechecked the final mapped locator in a disposable source copy: removing only its identity-validation call compiles and fails the 500-path property (0 passed, 1 failed) by permitting an alias update. The fixed worktree remains intact. Added the unchanged read contract as a fifth linked command; running all five with progress before full-gate retries."
  "2026-10-29T13:01:39.268Z",codex-agent,"Resource decision: retain the owner's requested split of focused local validation and full npm/Bun release certification in exact-head CI. The initial local npm aggregate exposed the ownership error-category regression (653 passed, 1 failed); that assertion is unchanged and all 18 read-contract cases now pass. Do not repeat long full suites on the shared host. CI now explicitly caps Cargo build jobs and Rust test threads at two, while retaining every release check and all four 100% coverage floors. Final CI run links and pending/completed counts will be maintained on PR 132 after the final tracker commit."
  "2026-10-29T13:05:30.174Z",codex-agent,"Final fixed-source linked verification passed all five commands: 5 integration + 20 admission library + 1 CLI boundary + 1 recovery + 18 existing read-contract tests = 45 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored. The unchanged ownership regression now passes alongside the new alias refusals. Pinned pm reports tracking_disabled; these measured results are retained here. All native filenames, shared-schema/settings interleavings, 132 published parity fixtures and 12 public-SDK identity fixtures remain covered."
  "2026-10-29T13:14:11.705Z",codex-agent,"Final local checks: cargo +1.90.0 clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -j 2 -- -D warnings passed. just crash-check passed harness typecheck/lint and all 82 crash-conformance tests (0 failures/skips/cancellations/todos), followed by successful main-history prefix validation (2 main-prefix histories, 2 branch-only histories) and retained evidence checks (20 receipts, 36 commits). Fresh fetch remains 0 commits behind origin/main; no merge is necessary. Public read-only corpus validation is being refreshed before releasing the claim and committing the final evidence."
  "2026-10-29T13:19:27.063Z",codex-agent,"Final public-data validation: read-only non-git copy of public main 91ac8a9, 89 SDK-certified items, 184 archived files / 4698201 bytes, 8 SDK preparation files and 192 frozen files. Native observations read 909472 source bytes and 99 entries; 4 intents produced 3 admitted / 1 refused, 427 input bytes / 1090 output bytes, 836 ms debug wall time. Every frozen byte and complete SDK-read item state remained unchanged, with no Git or Node on the native PATH. Final evidence: 45 linked tests, 116 mutation units, 32 scoped nightly tests with admission source at 100% lines/functions/regions/branches, 82 crash tests, lint and history/evidence checks passed. Both supplied round-2 findings and the discovered typed-refusal compatibility regression are addressed; no existing tests were weakened. Full npm/Bun/global coverage certification remains pending exact-head CI with two workers; final run links and counts are maintained at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/132. Existing schema/closure, local health and intermittent deadline follow-ups remain open. Releasing only this author's claim; item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T13:32:01.614Z",codex-agent,"Prior-head CI completed while this patch was being validated. Rust matrices passed, but the Bun aggregate found four uncovered regions / two lines in main's admission stdin/discovery error conversions; admission.rs itself remained 100%. Existing unit tests hit those paths only in the test binary. Reclaimed this item to add real-child-process refusals for unreadable stdin and missing tracker, preserving all four 100% floors and existing tests. Inspecting other prior-head failures before the next final push."
  "2026-10-29T13:46:53.822Z",codex-agent,"Added a real-child admission CLI regression using an inherited directory handle for unreadable stdin (including Windows backup-semantics directory opening) and a valid batch in a missing tracker. It passes with empty PATH/Git ceiling and preserves all tracker bytes. A targeted nightly run confirms both shipped/test run_with_io variants now execute the previously missed closing regions at main.rs:733 and :739 (each count 1), including both error-conversion closures. Related older Windows latency evidence (context p95 291.0006 ms vs 250 ms) is recorded on existing performance item pm-rust-wdj4; no latency ceiling was relaxed."
  "2026-10-29T14:05:35.177Z",codex-agent,"Supplementary fail-on-revert evidence: removing either main admission stdin/discovery refusal mapping independently compiles and fails the new real-process test (0 passed, 1 failed each); removing only the shared history-directory alias guard independently compiles and fails the new SDK regression (0 passed, 1 failed). Worktree production sources remained fixed throughout. Rebuilt fixed-source CLI and history tests pass, and all-target/all-feature Clippy with warnings denied passes. These two tests supplement the 45 linked tests; no earlier assertion was changed. All previous aggregate coverage misses are addressed by targeted cases while thresholds stay at 100%. Older Windows context timing remains tracked by pm-rust-wdj4 pending fresh CI."
  "2026-10-29T18:05:36.975Z",codex-agent,"CI repair round: fetched head 7ca5196; origin/main is fully included. GraphQL reports zero review threads and no CodeRabbit review bodies; the CodeRabbit issue comment states automatic review was skipped, with no Outside diff range findings. gh run view --log-failed returned empty output; downloaded job logs through the Actions API instead. All three failed aggregates reached the unchanged coverage gate and reported the same missing main/ownership regions. Investigating those exact paths and cancelled job logs; preserve product behavior and all thresholds."
  "2026-10-29T18:07:30.650Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed Actions annotations: Windows Rust exceeded 20 minutes during passing differential tests; Windows aggregate exceeded 35 minutes during the second instrumented test pass. Increase only Windows job budgets to 35 and 60 minutes respectively; assertions, latency limits and coverage floors stay unchanged. Native latency macOS never acquired a hosted runner (capacity constraint), had zero steps and no available log blob; this is infrastructure evidence, not a passing check. Add discovered-but-invalid settings to the real-process CLI refusal regression and directly test missing/present identities at the private lineage boundary, which shared filename validation now preempts in public mutation calls."
  "2026-10-29T18:11:34.595Z",codex-agent,"Focused stable tests both pass (2 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored). Sequential nightly branch instrumentation also passes both and records hits in the prior missing spans: main.rs 743:60-61 count 4; ownership.rs 456:16-458:11 count 1; the missing-key branch now executes both outcomes. These are scoped hits, not a global coverage claim. Whole-PR class audit reviewed shared snapshot capture, typed source propagation, filename lookup/recovery, governance preparation and the existing property/process tests; no additional product change is justified for this CI-only round. Revert builds are running serially in disposable non-git copies; the package sources remain fixed."
  "2026-10-29T18:17:17.512Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs completed in disposable non-git source copies: removing only ownership_parents missing-target guard compiled then failed ownership_lineage_scans_corpus_once (0 passed, 1 failed); replacing only the preview call typed-error propagation in run_with_io with an untyped I/O error compiled then failed admission_cli_read_and_discovery_refusals_are_typed (0 passed, 1 failed). The original production sources were never edited. Rebuilding fixed sources through both linked pm tests before the full unchanged just release-check. Ordinary-HOME strict health still has the previously tracked global-extension skew and shared-clone merge-driver drift; CI uses isolated clone-local installation. Changelog regenerated and checked successfully; no committed dist artifact exists in this Rust repository."
  "2026-10-29T18:28:18.928Z",codex-agent,"Fixed-source rebuild after both disposable mutations passed through pm test --run --only-index 6 and --only-index 7 --progress --timeout 1200: 2 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored. Pinned pm reports tracking_disabled, so this comment retains the measured result. Full just release-check is now running serially under a neutral HOME with credentials excluded, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 and RUST_TEST_THREADS=2. Format, history-prefix and added-line privacy checks pass; origin/main remains fully included."
  "2026-10-29T18:52:00.775Z",codex-agent,"Ready to push the CI-only repair: both focused regressions passed stable, instrumented and post-mutation pm runs; clippy and private documentation passed inside the full neutral-home gate. Current full-gate completed groups: 429 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored; claim/release and composed lifecycle parity cases have also passed within the ongoing group. The shared-host full oracle is substantially slower than CI, so push the verified patch to start exact-head platform validation while the same serial local gate continues. No required gate is removed or weakened. CI wait remains bounded to 30 minutes by queue policy; unfinished results will be recorded explicitly."
  "2026-10-29T19:24:21.127Z",codex-agent,"Bounded CI verification receipt for repair commit dc9005e: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/40935092438 has 0/10 completed jobs, states {'queued': 10}; CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/40935092309 is queued. Stopping CI polling at the existing 30-minute queue cutoff, 19:24 UTC. Fresh review inventory still has zero threads (no further pages) and no CodeRabbit review body. Main is fully included. Local neutral-home just release-check passed format, all-target Clippy and private documentation, then completed 7 Rust groups (473 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored). The log records 478 individual test passes including the unfinished group and 0 assertion failures before intentional interruption of this isolated run at the cutoff. Full local release/global coverage is NOT certified. Both targeted regressions pass stable, nightly and fixed-source pm runs (2 each); both behavioral mutants compile and fail 0 passed/1 failed. No assertions or thresholds were reduced. The final evidence-only push requires fresh exact-head CI; its run URLs and pending state are maintained on PR 132 without restarting the wait. Existing ordinary-HOME health findings remain tracked by pm-rust-vuwe; pinned pm test-result tracking remains disabled, so measured results are retained here. Releasing only this author's claim; keep the item in_progress for orchestrator verification."
